  "evidence": [
    "Current native/account/client/MFA/group admission, canonical selection, exact active bound device, provider metadata and completed legacy provenance are required at issuance and final publication.",
    "Ordinary employee root scopes work; company actors, foreign accounts, stale native proof, disabled/old clients and missing/foreign/expired/retired provider metadata fail.",
    "Lost bootstrap and refresh responses preserve their exact committed pair and hard deadline after native refresh; expired replay cannot renew its window.",
    "Same-operation bootstrap and concurrent refresh commit one pair/journal; a lookup that loses a race recovers the intervening winner.",
    "Malformed returned credentials, receipt/journal failure, late group/provider loss, cancellation/interruption and interrupted flags roll back actual writes.",
    "Expired access can refresh only while current native/provider and hard deadlines remain valid.",
    "Actual retained worker completion precedes group bootstrap/refresh; missing/foreign/incoherent completion rejects current and previous tokens while old identity/keys/credentials remain retired and runtime DRAINING."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No new HTTP route, Matrix gateway dispatch, shared DI binding, live migration, provider request or Mobile product caller.",
    "Before transport, return original Matrix IDs in an atomic bootstrap envelope and expose safe gateway revision metadata for recovery after a lost response exceeds replay expiry.",
    "Full publication fixture exercises worker use cases but is not an API or worker Spring application-context run. Both contexts are required when DI changes.",
    "Provider credential renewal, room authorization, coherent Mobile adoption and all54 communications acceptance groups remain unfinished.",
    "Normal phone28/live8b40/schema116 and Starter9959c1d remain unchanged."
  ]
